From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rtw88: preserve DIG gain when the RSSI sample is unavailable

Station iteration can return no RSSI sample while the driver still counts a
station, for example during removal or when collecting a station fails.
Do not use the U8_MAX no-sample sentinel to update linked DIG or its damping
history. Retain the last gain until a sample or the unlinked state is available.

Calculate the RSSI upper bound without narrowing the addition to u8. Otherwise
255 + 15 becomes 14, inverting the gain bounds and permitting a value below
the native DIG minimum. Valid samples and the unlinked coverage policy keep
their existing behavior.

Not submitted upstream.

Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/phy.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/phy.c
@@ -473,7 +473,7 @@
 	}
 
 	/* DIG MAX should be bounded by minimum RSSI with offset +15 */
-	dig_max = min_t(u8, dig_max, min_rssi + DIG_RSSI_GAIN_OFFSET);
+	dig_max = min_t(u16, dig_max, min_rssi + DIG_RSSI_GAIN_OFFSET);
 
 	*lower = clamp_t(u8, min_rssi, dig_min, dig_mid);
 	*upper = clamp_t(u8, *lower + DIG_RSSI_GAIN_OFFSET, dig_min, dig_max);
@@ -546,10 +546,13 @@
 	if (test_bit(RTW_FLAG_DIG_DISABLE, rtwdev->flags))
 		return;
 
+	linked = !!rtwdev->sta_cnt;
+	/* Station iteration can be empty before sta_cnt is decremented. */
+	if (linked && dm_info->min_rssi == U8_MAX)
+		return;
+
 	if (rtw_phy_dig_check_damping(dm_info))
 		return;
-
-	linked = !!rtwdev->sta_cnt;
 
 	fa_cnt = dm_info->total_fa_cnt;
 	pre_igi = dm_info->igi_history[0];
